From 60cec3c40c28050afc27edd403dc29e825271eb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 22:11:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 074/206] feat(shorebird): build the base snapshot's
 instructions table
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The last piece of the Deserializer's Shorebird surface that had a name but no
implementation. A patch replaces the app snapshot, so the base exists only as
raw mappings -- nothing has deserialized it, and there is no InstructionsTable
to hand the deserializer.

Everything InstructionsTable::New needs is in the base's own header, and that
header is five unsigned values at the start of the clustered stream: the same
five Deserialize reads. Which is what their cut-down Deserializer constructor
is for -- their DWARF has a second one taking only (Thread*, buffer, size,
data, instructions, offset), with no Kind, no InstructionsType and no
base-instruction parameters. A reader for a header and nothing else. That
constructor was recorded as unexplained two rounds ago.

The Deserializer now takes the pair their long constructor takes, in their
positions, and ReadProgramSnapshot supplies them. PrintShorebirdStats reports
the real state instead of a hardcoded "no".

Verified two ways. The "no" path is what every unpatched app takes and it runs
end to end. The "yes" path has no embedder here -- dartaotruntime never calls
Shorebird_SetBaseSnapshots, that is the Flutter shell's job -- so it was forced
once, by handing the app its own snapshot as the base:

    Has shorebird base instructions table: yes

which means SetupFromBuffer, VerifyVersionAndFeatures, the five varints, the
ImageReader and InstructionsTable::New all ran against a real snapshot, and the
program still produced the right output.

⚠️ That was an experiment, not a regression test. What is permanently covered
is the null path. Exercising the other one needs an embedder that sets base
snapshots, and adding a flag to dartaotruntime for it would be inventing API
rather than reproducing it.

90 of 90 shorebird tests; dd_runtime_check.sh and verify_reproduction.sh clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

